well we've seen another really  resounding defeat for the anti-abortion  crowd the Supreme Court yesterday said  that no you can't require in Louisiana  doctors who perform abortions to have  admitting privileges at area hospitals  that this effectively violates roe v  wade which is the precedent of note and  thus reminds us why this question of roe  v wade comes up so often when new  potential Supreme Court justices are  being vetted and questioned and what is  particularly interesting about this  decision is that it was a 5-4 decision  where the five the majority was made up  of the four more liberal justices and  Chief Justice John Roberts a moderate  conservative certainly no doubt about it  and we're going to talk more about Chief  Justice John Roberts and his legacy and  is sort of placed within the Supreme  Court on Thursday but for today I want  to talk about this decision that this  really is an important defeat for the  anti-choice movement that seeks to just  ban abortion make abortion illegal  despite the reality of course that  banning abortion reduces legal abortion  maybe at least in the state where it's  banned but it does not actually reduce  the number of women who figure out a way  to terminate a pregnancy and that's  another story that we've talked about  quite a bit on this program so the  reason this is an important decision is  that this is a common way to try to  restrict access to abortion the way it  works in this Louisiana law that was  struck down by the Supreme Court  yesterday and in other states the game  that they play essentially is you you  don't ban abortion per se but you  require doctors who perform abortions to  have admitting privileges at nearby  hospitals and the anti-abortion people  say that this is that the reason you do  this is well if a doctor performs an  abortion  and the patient needs to be hospitalized  it's important that the doctor have  admitting privileges so that that doctor  can continue providing care in the  hospital for the hospitalized abortion  patient now all of this is part of the  ruse that includes making abortion seem  like a far more risky medical procedure  than it actually is so a few realities  that we should keep in mind number one  hospitalizations after abortion are very  very rare number two even if one were  necessary a hospitalization the patient  would still be able to get care even if  the doctor that performed the abortion  doesn't have admitted admitting  privileges at the local hospital and  number three there are bureaucratic  reasons that sometimes make it difficult  for doctors who perform abortions to get  those admitting privileges so this is  essentially a trick from the anti-choice  crowd to make abortions more difficult  to obtain and maybe to dissuade people  from seeking them out in general so  understand how crazy this is five  doctors in all of Louisiana provide  abortions two of them have obtained  admitting privileges one in New Orleans  and one in Shreveport the Shreveport  doctor says he can't handle all of the  work alone and the trial judge concluded  that what this law in effect does is  reduce Louisiana to a single doctor in a  single clinic in New Orleans and that is  in practice a violation of roe v wade  that is ultimately what the Supreme  Court found that the roe v wade decision  from 1973 which is the precedent for so  much of the discussion about abortion  today would in practice be violated if  this law requiring admitting privileges  at local hospitals were to remain the  law of the land so this is relevant for  a few different reasons number one Chief  Justice John Roberts a George W Bush  appointee previously favored abortion  restrictions in two other abortion  related  we're going to talk more about him  momentarily but in this case john  roberts coming over with the majority in  defense of abortion rights number two  this is huge because everything is just  going wrong for this administration  donald trump as you may know now claims  to be against abortion he was in favor  of a woman's right to choose i believe  is for 67 or 68 years of life his  evangelical followers have fallen for it  hook line &amp; sinker  I guess they believe Trump is now  against abortion and this is another  decision that goes against Donald Trump  stated wishes if we believe that those  are actually his which wishes now let's  talk about Chief Justice John Roberts  because this is really for me the the  crux of the discussion that now is going  on on Friday I'm sorry on Thursday I'm  going to get into more detail about  whether Chief Justice John Roberts is a  moderate or a conservative of course he  was selected by george w bush but what I  really want you to understand about this  decision and the decision on daca last  week where John Roberts was also on the  side of we're not going to remove daca  for the reason the Trump administration  wants it removed these are technical  decisions these are not decisions where  John Roberts is coming over to the left  so to speak on the merits of abortion or  on the merits of daca what I mean by  that is in the daca case for example the  Trump administration just bungled their  case the Trump administration tried to  end daca by saying Barack Obama didn't  have the authority to put daca in place  via executive order the Supreme Court  said that's not a good argument the  supreme court john roberts they  correctly found that Obama did not  overstep Authority but it was not a  decision on the merits of daca and  similarly with this abortion decision  John Roberts is saying in a technical  sense the Louisiana law would violate  the precedent set by roe v wade it's a  technical decision it's not a decision  on the merits now will we take it of  course we will but what's important to  understand I mean look at even the LGB  discrimination case Roberts correctly  identified in a technical sense if you  allow an employer to discriminate on the  basis of sexual orientation or gender  identity by definition it is a  discriminatory act on the basis of sex  which is banned so what John Roberts did  it doesn't mean he made the wrong  decisions  it means he is simply getting the  technical question right it shows us  actually how insane the court is that  these decisions were not nine to zero  this decision on abortion should have  been nine to zero the law that Louisiana  wanted to pass on abortion obviously  violates roe v wade it should have been  a 9-0 decision so the message here  should not be who cares about judges we  got the right decision anyway even with  Chief Justice John Roberts who came over  and joined the liberal majority the  decision should have been nine to zero  and it shouldn't come down to one center  right justice deciding Oh precedent  matters precedent matters that's why we  need Joe Biden and not Donald Trump  choosing more justices because this  should have been should have been a 9-0  decision and then on Thursday we're  going to talk a little bit more sort of  about the political orientation of Chief  Justice John Roberts and other justices  on the court

